   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the general business law, in relation to auction requirements",
    "basePrintNo": "S8333",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8333-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §29, Gen Bus L (as proposed in S.4313-D/A.1730-D)",
    "lawSection": "General Business Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S8333\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act to amend the general business law, in relation to auction\nrequirements\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nTo add an exemption of auctions conducted by or on behalf of government\nentities from the provisions of the recently passed auction requirements\nestablished in Section twenty-nine of the General Business Law.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of this Chapter amendment would lower the population thresh-\nold of counties affected by this statute from 200,000 to 45,000 people.\n\nSection two states that the new paragraph f of subdivision eight of\nsection twenty-nine would exempt auction or auctions of certain highway\nequipment conducted by or on behalf of the federal government, or the\nstate, its agencies, bureaus, boards, commissions and authorities, or\nany political subdivision of the state, or the agencies and authorities\nof any such subdivision from the \"Requirements for Auctions\" section of\nthe General Business Law.  Section twenty-three of the General Business\nLaw, Automobile Auctioneers, has a similar automobile exemption for\nauctions by governmental entities.\n\nSection three of the bill would provide for the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIt has become clear during the legislative process that S.4113D/ A.1730D\nwent through that many more counties in the State of New York would\nbenefit enormously from the provisions provided in this chapter.\n\nIn addition, the auctioning of motor vehicles has a long established\nsystem regulated under section twenty-three of the general business law\nthat provides for the exclusion of auctions conducted by the state, its\nagencies, political subdivisions, and other entities. This bill recog-\nnizes that governmental auctions are different from those performed in\nthe art market and provides for language similar to the automobile\nauctioneer statute that will exempt those auctions from the provisions\nof requirements for auctions as established in a chapter of the laws of\n2010, as proposed in legislative bill numbers S.4313D and A.1730D.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis bill would take effect on the same date as a chapter of the laws of\n2010, in relation to auction requirements.\n\n",
